  "description": "XUBHOR crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C102 H143 N6 Nd4 O17 S10 3+,2(C3 H7 N1 O1),3(N1 O3 1-),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd1B (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd2B (Nd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.675-5.266 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.78-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd4(OH){(C40H44O4S4)(C3H7NO)}2(C3H7NO)6(C2H6SO)2](NO3)3·3H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
